# THE REPO IS MIXED, AND THE THREE PROJECT FILES ARE NOT.
#
# script.gs and app.html are LF throughout and must stay that way. The 37 files
# they were merged from were mixed THREE ways — most .html were CRLF, Code.gs
# was LF, and two .gs carried a lone CR as a line terminator — and every tool
# that has ever anchored on a spelled-out line ending in this repo has broken.
#
# `text eol=lf` makes git write LF into the working tree on every platform, so
# an editor on Windows cannot quietly convert them back on the next save. This
# is the mechanical form of a rule that was previously only written down.

script.gs        text eol=lf
app.html         text eol=lf
appsscript.json  text eol=lf

# Everything else keeps whatever it has: the harnesses read deleted files out
# of git and normalise line endings themselves, and re-encoding history would
# change what they compare against.
*.md             text
tests/*.js       text
